<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Raigarh State</h1><p class="st-meta">1625 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Raigarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Gond-ruled state of eastern Chhattisgarh whose music-loving ruler made it a centre of Kathak dance.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Raigarh was ruled by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raj-gond">Raj Gond</a> dynasty whose traditions say they came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrapur">Chanda</a> (Chandrapur). The register dates the state to around 1625. It was later a dependency of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Bhonsles of Nagpur</a> before passing under British paramountcy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled a territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> fields and forests along the Mand river. Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakradhar-singh">Chakradhar Singh</a>, who reigned from 1924, gathered leading musicians and dancers at his court and wrote treatises on dance, giving rise to the Raigarh gharana of Kathak.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Raigarh merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces and Berar</a> in 1948, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>. Since 2000 it has been in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, where the annual Chakradhar Samaroh festival of music recalls its court.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/raigarh-state.jpg" alt="Raigarh State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Raigarh_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1625 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Raigarh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chakradhar Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chhattisgarhi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Raigarh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1786&amp;focus=raigarh-state" aria-label="Raigarh State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6916 1369 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Raigarh State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7236 1625L7364 1602M7236 1625L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7236 1625h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7236 1625h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1786&amp;focus=raigarh-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
